## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic per-tenant policy enforcement in a Saga-driven architecture, including how to store, fetch, and react to runtime feature flags, and how to handle compensation when policy constraints change mid-flight. It also probes read-model migration strategies in an event-sourced, CQRS system.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant policy store with versioned flags
- Saga step gating and compensation
- Runtime policy changes and drift handling
- Read-model migrations with event-versioning
- Idempotency and outbox patterns

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator check before executing a step
function canRun(tenantId, sagaName, stepId) {
  const policy = policyStore.get(tenantId, sagaName, stepId);
  return policy?.enabled !== false;
}
```

```javascript
// React to policy changes: enqueue compensation if a gated step becomes invalid later
async function onPolicyChange(tenantId, sagaName, stepId, newPolicy) {
  if (!newPolicy.enabled) await compensationStore.enqueue({ tenantId, sagaName, stepId });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test dynamic gating across thousands of tenants? 
- How would you ensure read-model migrations remain backward-compatible while policy flags evolve?

## Why This Question Is Asked

Tests the ability to design scalable, highly available job queues with tenant isolation and live rebalancing.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant sharding and hot-tenant handling
- Replica synchronization and consistency models (CP vs AP)
- Online shard rebalancing with lease-based ownership
- Delivery semantics (at-least-once vs exactly-once) and deduplication
- Failure modes, observability, and testing under churn

## Code Example

```javascript
// Acquire shard lease for a tenant
const shardHandle = await acquireShardLease(tenantId);

// Enqueue job to tenant's shard
async function enqueueJob(tenantId, job) {
  const shardId = computeShard(tenantId, job.id);
  const shard = await getShardOwner(shardId);
  return shard.enqueue({ tenantId, job, timestamp: Date.now() });
}

// Idempotent job processing
async function processJob(job, shard) {
  const acquired = await shard.acquireLock(job.id, leaseDuration);
  if (!acquired) return { status: 'skipped' };

  const processed = await checkProcessed(job.id);
  if (processed) return { status: 'duplicate', jobId: job.id };

  await executeJob(job);
  await markProcessed(job.id);
  await shard.releaseLock(job.id);

  return { status: 'completed', jobId: job.id };
}
```

